    "description": "<h3><strong>Description</strong></h3>\n<p>This dataset is a <strong>replicated copy</strong> of the <em>Medical Segmentation Decathlon (MSD) Spleen Dataset</em>, created solely to comply with <strong>PLOS ONE&rsquo;s data availability requirements</strong>.<br>The original dataset was developed and is maintained by the Medical Segmentation Decathlon organizers. Full details and the official source can be accessed here:<br><strong>Official Website:</strong> <a href=\"http://medicaldecathlon.com/\" target=\"_new\" rel=\"noopener\">http://medicaldecathlon.com/</a><br><strong>Original License and Terms:</strong> Please refer to the official MSD repository for licensing and usage conditions.</p>\n<p>No modifications have been made to the original data other than repackaging for hosting on a stable repository (Zenodo).</p>\n<h3><strong>Citation</strong></h3>\n<p>If you use this dataset, please cite the original source:<br>Antonelli, M., et al. (2022). Medical Segmentation Decathlon. <em>Nature Communications</em>. <a target=\"_new\" rel=\"noopener\">DOI: 10.1038/s41467-022-30695-9<br></a></p>\n<h3><strong>Notes</strong></h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>This replication has been uploaded exclusively to fulfill journal requirements.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>All intellectual property rights belong to the original authors/organization.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
